            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a Vac on a Platform You Do Not Own</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A cordless vac without batteries does nothing, and packs and a charger can cost as much as the vac. Unless you are switching platforms anyway, buy the best vac on the batteries you already have, even if another brand's model looks slightly better on paper.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting the Headline Runtime</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Published runtimes usually assume the largest battery the brand sells and sometimes a low power setting. Scale the figure by amp-hours to estimate what your own packs will deliver, and expect a little less in a cold garage or on heavy material.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Choosing a 1-1/4 Inch Hose for Bulky Debris</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Compact vacs with small hoses are excellent for dust and cars but clog on leaves, wood chips and drywall scraps. If garage and yard debris is your main job, choose a vac with a 1-7/8 inch hose.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Vacuuming Water With the Dry Filter Fitted</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A paper or pleated filter is ruined by water and can let moisture reach the motor. Fit the foam sleeve or remove the dry filter for wet pickup, exactly as the manual describes, and dry everything before storing.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming Every HEPA Label Means the Same Thing</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                True HEPA is rated at 99.97 percent at 0.3 microns. Some cordless vacs use filters rated lower or at larger particle sizes. If you sand drywall or cut concrete indoors, read the actual filter rating before you buy.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

